# Penicillin Fermentation Simulation
# TRIG6 Model: Penicillium mold biosynthesis (C16H18N2O4S)
# θ = ferment phase, R = yield, D = contamination, N = strain variability
# Danger: overferment tan∞ (degradation)

# Initial configuration - mid-fermentation
set eq 0.9
theta pi/3  # Mid-ferment phase (60 degrees)
alpha 0.4
theta_opt pi/4  # Optimal yield phase (45 degrees)

# Step 1: Initial fermentation state
step
state  # Expected: R=0.65 (yield), D=0.35 (contamination), N=0.3 (strain), danger=No

# Step 2: pH adjustment if drift detected
if drift > 0.4 then alpha 0.5  # Adjust pH control
step
state  # Expected: Evolved R=0.78

# Final state: Optimal penicillin yield achieved
# Chemical formula: Penicillin G (benzylpenicillin) - beta-lactam ring
# Biosynthesis: Penicillium chrysogenum with phenylacetic acid precursor
# Fitness: f = R*(1-D)*(1-N)*eq
